  ("IDEA-PKG-CONFIG-REGRESSION" . (
    (priority . 9.5)
    (description . "New 2026-08-18: bun run tauri build, which produced working .deb+.rpm bundles earlier the same day (see IDEA-BUN-TAURI-VALIDATION/IDEA-PUSH-BUN-MIGRATION), now fails the whole build (not just AppImage) with 'The pkg-config command could not be found' while building gio-sys/gobject-sys — inside the same guix time-machine + shell -m manifest.scm environment, pkg-config IS in manifest.scm's package list. Not caused by the xdg-utils manifest experiment (failed identically after that was fully reverted). Likely a Guix profile/store state issue (stale profile, guix channel drift between the two runs) rather than a real regression in this repo's config. Confirmed `which pkg-config` DOES resolve inside the guix shell (/gnu/store/.../profile/bin/pkg-config, version 0.29.2, same profile hash the failing build script printed) — so pkg-config is present and the shell's PATH is fine; the failure is specifically inside the gio-sys/gobject-sys build-script subprocess not seeing it, which points at cargo build-script PATH inheritance or a concurrent-build/profile-locking race rather than a missing package. Next step: rerun the exact same tauri build a second time back-to-back (no manifest change in between) to see if it's reproducible or a one-off race.")
    (done . ())
